-- Shaders X | Native cinematic environments | 1.0
-- Client-side. Run as a LocalScript (StarterPlayerScripts) or through your client loader.
-- One self-contained file: no downloaded code, hidden properties or graphics-engine overrides.
-- API returned at the bottom: Activate(name), DisableAll(), SetQuality(name), SetSkybox(bool), Destroy().
--
-- Sky images are complete six-face sets, checked against Roblox image metadata and thumbnails.
-- Each set is also preloaded on demand in the running experience. If permission/loading fails,
-- keep the original sky while applying the preset's native atmosphere and clouds independently.
-- SkyboxManager below records the verified face mapping; no model/decal IDs masquerade as textures.
-- Native APIs: https://create.roblox.com/docs/environment/atmosphere
-- https://create.roblox.com/docs/environment/skybox | https://create.roblox.com/docs/effects/post-processing
-- Aurora is a small layered Beam simulation, not a photographic panorama or GPU shader.
-- Volumetric Fog uses Atmosphere scattering, not ray-marched local volumetrics.
-- Rendering quality, texture resolution and LightingStyle remain controlled by Roblox/the experience.
-- Games may subsequently replace Lighting values/effects. We deliberately do not fight game scripts
-- every frame; reselect a preset to reapply it. Foreign camera effects are never disabled.
-- No physics, character, movement or gameplay properties are touched.

